  "notes": "Tharaka uses a 7-vowel system typical of the Meru-Tharaka group. The circumflex vowels î and û represent /ɪ/ and /ʊ/. Consonants b and g are typically fricatives /β/ and /ɣ/ between vowels. Prenasalized stops (mb, nd, nj, nk, nt) are treated as single phonemes. The apostrophe is used for elision (e.g., n'ata) and is not mapped to a phoneme.",
